  "body": "What happens: a 2D Adaptive operation on the biggest fig8 patch (`testdata/models/fig8.step`), with the Boundary group open and Containment at its default, shows no area fill. `boundary_viz::preview_fill` gives `None`.\n\nEvidence (found while I worked on #2762, at a8d923108 plus the #2762 fix):\n- `operation::region_of` gives 12 loops. Two loops are real: 509 points (2827 mm2) and 365 points (707 mm2).\n- The other 10 loops have 3 points each. Their areas are between 5e-9 and 1.5e-7 mm2. Two of them are clockwise.\n- `Region::triangles` refuses with `Invalid(\"hole outside any boundary\")`, because a clockwise sliver has no parent loop.\n- The same loops sent again through `Loop::new` and `Region::new` triangulate (870 triangles, area equal to the region area). Thus the slivers come from the constructor that `region_of` uses for this case, not from the triangulator.\n- Containment Inside on the same patch gives 2 loops and a correct fill.\n\nExpected: the region that `region_of` gives has no loop of near-zero area, or the fill ignores such loops. The outline and the fill agree with what generation cuts.\n\nDone means: the default-containment preview of the biggest fig8 patch has a fill. A test pins it. If the slivers also reach generation, the fix removes them there too, or a follow-up names that.\n",
